@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+id: dl-005-cancellation-refund-policy-validation-scope
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancellation: refund policy, validation, scope"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Customers ask to cancel bookings. `cancel(bookingId, at)` must return `{ bookingId, refund }`, free the
+equipment, and work only once per booking. The request does not state the refund rule.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Refund = the booking's whole total when `at` is strictly before the booking's start; 0 at or after the
+  start. No partial tiers: none were specified, and none are invented.
+- `at` must be an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp (`...Z`, any time of day); it is a parameter, never the clock.
+- An unknown booking id, an already cancelled booking, or an invalid `at` throws; a failed call changes
+  nothing.
+- A cancelled booking is kept (booking ids stay sequential) but no longer clashes in `book` nor hides
+  items in `availability`. A cancellation after the start still frees the item, with no refund.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The refund rule is a business assumption to confirm with the school; changing it is local to `cancel`.
